<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Auteini</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of western Ireland named by Ptolemy, usually placed in Galway or Mayo and possibly linked with the later Uaithni.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Auteini, or Autini, are listed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geography-ptolemy">Ptolemy's Geography</a> of about 150 on the west coast of Ireland, between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nagnatae">Nagnatae</a> to the north and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gangani-ireland">Gangani (Ireland)</a> to the south, roughly in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galway">Galway</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-mayo">Mayo</a>. Ptolemy's Irish data came from earlier maritime reports and are imprecise.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is known of their rulers or society. Their name is often compared with the Uaithni, a population group recorded in early medieval Ireland in north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-tipperary">Tipperary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a>, which could indicate a later movement south or a mistaken placing by Ptolemy, but the identification remains conjecture.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Auteini do not appear in later records. The west of Ireland where Ptolemy placed them later formed part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-connacht">Kingdom of Connacht</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/auteini.jpg" alt="Auteini" width="320" height="407"><figcaption>Image: Paul S · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ptolemy_ire.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Goidelic Celtic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Autini</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=auteini" aria-label="Auteini on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4506 350 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Auteini lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4826 606h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4826 606h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ireland. <a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=auteini">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

